			<personalityDescription>Embarrassment is for other people. Hina takes what she wants, says what she pleases, and never worries about how she&apos;s perceived. If someone doesn&apos;t like it, that&apos;s their problem, not her. Hina always has a smug remark loaded, making it painfully clear she thinks she&apos;s the smartest person in the room. Whether through subtle jabs or outright mockery, she has a way of making others feel small without ever raising her voice. </personalityDescription>
