			<personalityDescription>Dewitt doesn&apos;t force people to do what he wants - he makes them want to do it. A well-placed word here, a gentle push there, and suddenly, they&apos;re making decisions that just happen to work out in Dewitt&apos;s favor. It&apos;s not his fault he&apos;s so persuasive. Dewitt is up before dawn, already running drills while the rest of the squad is barely conscious. &quot;Morning is when the real warriors prepare,&quot; he says, sipping a steaming-hot cup of coffee while everyone else groans. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Doesn&apos;t force - makes them want it. Persuasion is their sharpest weapon.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
