			<personalityDescription>Callum measures everything - risks, rewards, weaknesses - before making a move. To him, emotion is just another factor to manipulate, and hesitation is a flaw he has no intention of indulging. Callum preps his weapons the exact same way before every mission. Field strips, recalibrates, reloads-even if they don&apos;t need it. &quot;Why do you keep doing that?&quot; someone asks. He shrugs. &quot;Routine keeps you sharp.&quot; What he doesn&apos;t say? Without it, the battlefield feels too unpredictable. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 52%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Emotion is leverage, not weakness. Hesitation isn&apos;t tolerated.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
