			<performanceExamScore>48</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>For Haniyya, combat isn&apos;t just a job - it&apos;s a sport, and she is always eager to rack up a higher score. She treats every battle like a game of &quot;who can make the biggest explosion,&quot; cracking jokes over comms while turning enemies into scrap. If war ever ended, Haniyya would probably be bored to death. Haniyya doesn&apos;t believe in fair fights - she believes in surviving. She&apos;ll lie, cheat, betray, and destroy without hesitation, because in her world, there&apos;s no room for second place. If someone isn&apos;t strong enough to keep up, they don&apos;t deserve to be here. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 53%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Treats war like sport. Competes for kill count. Jokes over comms.&lt;br&gt;- Fair fights are for fools. Ruthless, deceptive, and deadly efficient.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
