			<personalityDescription>If Gideon isn&apos;t in control, he isn&apos;t comfortable. He orchestrates every move, dictates every step, and ensures that nothing happens without his approval - because, in his mind, no one else can be trusted to do it right. Gideon mentions his crime like it&apos;s a funny story - until you realize the punchline never comes. He tries to pass it off as a mistake, but the guilt in his eyes says it&apos;s something far worse. &quot;Yeah, I made a bad call. Could&apos;ve gone better. Could&apos;ve gone... a lot better.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 45%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Needs full control to function. Dictates every step, permits nothing unsupervised.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
