			<performanceExamScore>50</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>When everything goes wrong, Dorothy is the one still standing, ready to fight. She charges into danger not because it&apos;s easy, but because someone has to - and if that means being the last one out, so be it. The repair bays stink of sweat and burnt wiring, the barracks always reek of gun oil, and the battlefield is worse. Dorothy fights the stink of war with an arsenal of lavender, sandalwood, and citrus candles. Her squadmates mock her - until they realize her bunk actually smells nice. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Last one out. Takes the risk so others don&apos;t have to. Anchor in chaos.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
