			<performanceExamScore>52</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>To Sammer, hesitation is just another word for failure. He throws caution aside, charging headlong into danger with raw aggression and an utter disregard for self-preservation. If survival means second-guessing, then maybe survival isn&apos;t worth it. Sammer sees no reason to dance around the truth. Whether it&apos;s giving orders, delivering bad news, or calling someone out on their mistakes, he doesn&apos;t soften the blow - because in his mind, reality doesn&apos;t come with padding. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 56%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Ignores self-preservation. Sees hesitation as death. Risk of early burnout.&lt;br&gt;- Truth hits hard. So do they. Doesnt apologize for either.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
