			<personalityDescription>Once In-Young commits to something, that&apos;s the end of the discussion. No argument, no persuasion, no force in the universe is enough to shake her resolve once she&apos;s made up her mind. In-Young treats the truth as optional. If a lie gets her what she wants faster, she won&apos;t hesitate to spin a story, twist the facts, or leave out just enough details to shift things in her favor. </personalityDescription>
