			<performanceExamScore>46</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Fear is for the weak, and Ludvig has no patience for it. They throw themself into battle with wild abandon, ignoring risks and consequences. Whether it&apos;s bravery or a death wish, sooner or later, it&apos;s going to catch up with them. Subtlety? Restraint? Ludvig&apos;s never heard of them. If one LRM is good, twenty are better. If a fight can be won cleanly, they&apos;ll still make sure it ends in a glorious fireball. Everything they do is bigger, louder, and more chaotic than it ever needed to be. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 48%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Ignores risk entirely. Bravery or death wish - hard to tell.&lt;br&gt;- Bigger, louder, messier - never clean, never subtle.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
