			<personalityDescription>Atsumori doesn&apos;t just win - he makes sure everyone knows he won. He taunts enemies, overplays his hand, and takes flashy risks just for the sake of proving he can. He&apos;s good - he just might not be as good as he thinks. Atsumori knows exactly what to say to get people on his side, but his words rarely match his true intentions. He smiles, flatters, and makes promises, but beneath it all, he&apos;s only looking out for himself. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 49%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Wins loud. Risks big to prove a point - might not be worth it.&lt;br&gt;- All charm, no substance. Says the right things, means none of them.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
