			<personalityDescription>Louise rarely takes others seriously, rolling their eyes at concerns they don&apos;t find valid. Whether it&apos;s a risky plan, a personal grievance, or a suggestion they think is dumb, they shut it down with a snide remark and move on. No strategy is ever good enough for Louise. They pick apart every formation, every maneuver, every decision. &quot;That&apos;s a weak flank. That exit is a death trap. This timing is off by at least three seconds.&quot; It&apos;s exhausting - but more than once, their nitpicking has saved lives. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 50%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Eye-rolls and shutdowns. Doesn&apos;t bother pretending to care.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
