			<personalityDescription>Bill isn&apos;t afraid of consequences - they simply don&apos;t think about them. They jump before looking, commit before planning, and laugh in the face of disaster, because for them, the thrill of the risk is always worth it. Bill doesn&apos;t just dislike &apos;Meks - they resent them. The destruction, the collateral damage, the way they turn wars into who has the bigger machine instead of who actually has skill. &quot;People used to fight with their own hands,&quot; they mutter. &quot;Now they just let a fusion engine do the killing for them.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 45%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- No thoughts of consequence. Laughs at disaster, races toward it.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
