			<personalityDescription>Finn could probably win more fights if they didn&apos;t spend so much time starting them. Whether it&apos;s trash-talking over comms or throwing the first punch in a negotiation, they seem to believe the best way to solve a problem is by making it someone else&apos;s problem. Fist first. Finn locks onto their objectives with laser precision. Distractions, doubts, and setbacks don&apos;t faze them - once they set their sights on something, they follow through until the job is done. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 53%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Starts problems just to end them violently. First to swing, last to think.&lt;br&gt;- Locks in on goals and doesn&apos;t let go. Setbacks don&apos;t register - only results.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
