			<performanceExamScore>51</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Why wait when you can act? Tomás leaps before looking, speaks before thinking, and never backs down from a challenge. Whether it&apos;s a high-stakes battle or a bad bet, he is always rolling the dice, just to see what happens. Tomás isn&apos;t just skeptical - he&apos;s haunted by past failures. The cutting-edge weapons that jammed, the prototype that failed, the experimental implants that fried their users from the inside out. He doesn&apos;t hate innovation - he just knows that in war, new means untested, and untested means deadly. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 54%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Leaps into trouble for the thrill. Makes chaos just to see the outcome.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
