			<personalityDescription>Aida charges into danger without a second thought, unshaken by enemy fire or overwhelming odds. She believes fear is a distraction and meets every challenge with unwavering resolve. Aida whistles while mounting the DropShip, while advancing through enemy fire, while standing over the wreckage of a downed opponent. It&apos;s never frantic - always slow, steady, calm. Her lance isn&apos;t sure if it&apos;s confidence or insanity, but when the whistling stops, they know things have gone very wrong. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 54%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Charges in without hesitation. Treats fear as noise, not warning.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
