			<personalityDescription>Mary sees rules as obstacles, not boundaries. If there&apos;s a shortcut to be taken or a loophole to exploit, she&apos;ll find it - ethics and fairness be damned. Mary is always doing something, even when she doesn&apos;t need to be. If she&apos;s talking to you, she&apos;s also reorganizing crates, flipping a pen between her fingers, or double-checking inventory counts that don&apos;t actually need to be checked. She calls it &quot;efficient multitasking.&quot; Everyone else calls it &quot;exhausting to watch.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 34%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Treats rules like suggestions. Never plays clean.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
