			<personalityDescription>Pain, exhaustion, even death - none of it matters. Shanley will see his mission through to the bitter end, no matter the cost. Stubbornness and sheer willpower keep him standing long after others have fallen. Every skirmish, every engagement, every ambush reminds him of a past war. &quot;This is just like the Hesperus II siege, different scale, same mistakes,&quot; he mutters, adjusting his sights. His lance has learned that whenever he starts recounting military history mid-skirmish, it&apos;s either a sign of his confidence - or a really bad omen. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 49%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Pain means nothing. Mission above all. Stands long after support falls.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
