			<performanceExamScore>47</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>For Bhuvadvasu, hesitation is just another form of failure. He throws himself into danger without a second thought, making split-second calls that can mean brilliance or disaster - but either way, he never slows down. Before every battle, Bhuvadvasu insists on running a final check. Formation assignments? Confirmed. Backup comms? Verified. Extraction routes? Plotted and re-plotted. &quot;The battlefield is messy enough,&quot; he mutters. &quot;No reason we have to be.&quot; The others may roll their eyes, but when things go wrong, his plans are why they make it out alive. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 49%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Hesitation rejected. Decisions made mid-charge. High risk, high volatility.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
