			<personalityDescription>Anne doesn&apos;t believe in dead ends - only obstacles waiting to be overcome. No setback, failure, or rejection is enough to make them walk away from something they&apos;ve committed to. Anne&apos;s indifference isn&apos;t an act - it&apos;s survival. They&apos;ve seen too much, lost too much, and learned that the only way to endure is to stop feeling altogether. The universe burns, but they stopped worrying about the flames a long time ago. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 46%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Sees setbacks as challenges, not endings. Keeps advancing.&lt;br&gt;- Hollow eyes. Doesnt hate you - just can&apos;t be bothered to.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
