			<personalityDescription>Teamwork is just a means to an end for Moritz. He&apos;ll play along as long as it benefits him, but the moment there&apos;s something to gain, he won&apos;t hesitate to take more than his fair share. Moritz tells and retells his tales of bravery because he needs them to matter. He needs people to see him as fearless, as someone who never wavered, as someone worth remembering. Because deep down, he knows that in war, the forgotten are already dead. </personalityDescription>
