			<personalityDescription>Luke treats the impossible like an invitation. He never slows down, never looks back, and never lets fear dictate his choices - because, to him, fear is just an excuse he refuses to entertain. Luke knows that most fights don&apos;t matter, that most enemies are just faceless obstacles. But there&apos;s one. One that is different. One that is personal. This rivalry is the only thing left that still feels like it has meaning. &quot;They&apos;ll either kill me, or I&apos;ll kill them. And that&apos;s the only thing I know for sure anymore.&quot; </personalityDescription>
