			<personalityDescription>Some call it paranoia; Dana calls it survival. They keep their eyes open, their mind sharp, and their instincts honed, because the moment they let their guard down, they know that&apos;s when disaster will strike. Dana doesn&apos;t rush - they refine. Every plan, every shot, every move is calculated and practiced until it&apos;s second nature. They believe that mastery comes from discipline, and discipline comes from doing the work no one else is willing to. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 34%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Calls it survival, not paranoia. Guard never drops, not for a second.&lt;br&gt;- Repetition breeds mastery. Refines until perfection is habit.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
