			<personalityDescription>For Demaci, hesitation is just another form of failure. He throws himself into danger without a second thought, making split-second calls that can mean brilliance or disaster - but either way, he never slows down. Demaci doesn&apos;t just see the game being played - he plays it better than everyone else. He spots weaknesses, exploits blind spots, and reads people like open books. By the time others realize they&apos;ve been outmaneuvered, it&apos;s already too late. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 53%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Hesitation rejected. Decisions made mid-charge. High risk, high volatility.&lt;br&gt;- Playing three games at once and winning all of them.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
