			<personalityDescription>Hua-ding measures success in wealth and power, and they refuse to settle for anything less than everything. If there&apos;s something to gain, they&apos;ll take it - no matter the cost. Hua-ding survives. They&apos;ve survived everything. They never charge in, never take unnecessary risks, never make the fatal mistakes their comrades do. But survival comes at a cost - they&apos;re always the one left standing, always the one pulling bodies from wreckage, always the one left to bury the dead. They wonder if, one day, caution won&apos;t be enough. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 51%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Doesnt take a slice - takes the whole damn pie.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
