			<performanceExamScore>46</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Marciano doesn&apos;t just see the game being played - he plays it better than everyone else. He spots weaknesses, exploits blind spots, and reads people like open books. By the time others realize they&apos;ve been outmaneuvered, it&apos;s already too late. Marciano writes because it&apos;s the only way to process the things he&apos;s seen. The words are sharp, brutal, and honest in a way that scares even him sometimes. &quot;If I don&apos;t put it down on paper, it stays in my head. And trust me - you don&apos;t want it staying there.&quot; </personalityDescription>
