			<personalityDescription>Chelsea knows exactly how to turn on the charm, and she&apos;s not shy about using it. Whether it&apos;s smooth talk, playful banter, or lingering glances, she thrives on attraction and never passes up an opportunity for a little fun. Chelsea&apos;s seen too many comrades die. She&apos;s stopped trying to make real connections with people - they never last. But animals? They don&apos;t ask questions. They don&apos;t make promises they can&apos;t keep. And when Chelsea whispers to a half-starved dog before a skirmish, telling it to run and hide, it&apos;s not because she&apos;s worried about the mutt. It&apos;s because, deep down, she knows it&apos;ll outlive her. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 50%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Weaponizes charm. Knows how to smile and take what they want.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
