			<personalityDescription>Jacqueline always takes the time to think about how their actions affect others. Whether it&apos;s checking in on their comrades, giving credit where it&apos;s due, or offering help without being asked, they make sure people feel valued and respected. Jacqueline never trusts supply lines. They&apos;ve got ration bars stuffed in their boots, emergency packs taped onto their helmet, and a hidden stash of canned food somewhere in the barracks. &quot;You never know when things go bad,&quot; they say. The way they say it makes people wonder if they&apos;re speaking from experience. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 52%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Keeps an eye on the squad - remembers who skipped rations, who didn&apos;t sleep.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
