			<personalityDescription>Milorad doesn&apos;t waste time on fair deals when an unfair one gets him more. He plays on desperation, weaknesses, and ambition, twisting every situation to ensure that, in the end, Milorad is the one who profits most. Milorad&apos;s tone alone is enough to set people on edge. Whether it&apos;s the slow, deliberate way he corrects others or the way he smirks when they struggle, he makes it painfully clear that he thinks he&apos;s leagues ahead of everyone else. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 52%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- If theres a win to be had, they&apos;ll take the lion&apos;s share and call it fair.&lt;br&gt;- Even praise feels like punishment. Might make enemies just by talking.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
