			<personalityDescription>Chris doesn&apos;t just avoid conflict - he redirects it. A well-placed phrase, a subtle shift in tone, or a carefully chosen silence can turn an argument into an opportunity, ensuring that things go his way without force. Chris doesn&apos;t just dislike &apos;Meks - he resents them. The destruction, the collateral damage, the way they turn wars into who has the bigger machine instead of who actually has skill. &quot;People used to fight with their own hands,&quot; he mutters. &quot;Now they just let a fusion engine do the killing for them.&quot; </personalityDescription>
