			<performanceExamScore>45</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Caution is boring, and Badar would rather go down in flames than play it safe. He lives for the thrill of insane risks, treating the battlefield like a proving ground for just how crazy he can get - and somehow, he usually pulls it off. Badar doesn&apos;t count for fun. He counts because it&apos;s the only thing keeping him grounded. He tracks shots, seconds, distances - anything but the number of bodies left behind. The moment he stops counting, he knows he&apos;ll have to face those numbers too. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 51%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Thrill-seeker. Battlefield is their playground. Somehow survives - so far.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
