			<personalityDescription>Lowell doesn&apos;t do diplomacy, small talk, or patience. Every interaction is laced with an edge of hostility, as if he&apos;s daring the world to give him a reason to lash out. &quot;Being late is the fastest way to get killed.&quot; Lowell drills it into every rookie he meets. In war, seconds matter - hesitate, delay, miss your mark, and you&apos;re dead. His lance jokes that he sets his watch five minutes fast just to make sure he&apos;s never late. They&apos;re only half wrong. It&apos;s ten minutes. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 55%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Always confrontational. Anticipates violence, welcomes it.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
