			<personalityDescription>Zale&apos;s hunger for success, control, or destruction knows no limits. He takes and takes, pushing himself and others past the breaking point, never feeling like it&apos;s enough. His drive isn&apos;t ambition - it&apos;s addiction. Zale has seen too much to care about petty concerns. He ignores emotions, disregards complaints, and barely acknowledges those he considers beneath him. If someone isn&apos;t immediately useful, they might as well not exist. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Pushes past limits like they don&apos;t exist. Burnout risk? Doesnt care.&lt;br&gt;- Doesn&apos;t see people - just obstacles or irrelevancies.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
