			<performanceExamScore>49</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>For Orlantha, compromise is just another word for weakness. She sticks to her principles, strategies, and orders with unwavering determination, even when logic - or survival - suggests a different path. Orlantha collects junk. Old playing cards, broken holovids, half-melted action figures. She swears each one has a story, even if it&apos;s just &quot;found it in a burned-out bunker.&quot; Some say it&apos;s a harmless habit, but others worry - because Orlantha never throws anything away, even the stuff that should be forgotten. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 51%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Sees compromise as failure. Principles trump survival instinct.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
