			<performanceExamScore>47</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Subtlety has never been Sloan&apos;s strong suit. She speaks in hard facts and brutal honesty, never sugarcoating her words or wasting time on delicate phrasing. If someone doesn&apos;t like it, that&apos;s their problem. Sloan doesn&apos;t trust allied command, mission planners, or anyone not risking their own skin. She&apos;s seen too many decisions made by people who never have to face the consequences. &quot;Oh, great, another &apos;brilliant strategy&apos; from someone sitting in an underground, reinforced bunker.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 49%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Subtle as artillery. Doesnt care who flinches.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
