			<personalityDescription>Subtlety? Restraint? Sharon&apos;s never heard of them. If one LRM is good, twenty are better. If a fight can be won cleanly, they&apos;ll still make sure it ends in a glorious fireball. Everything they do is bigger, louder, and more chaotic than it ever needed to be. Even in the heat of war, Sharon never loses sight of the people fighting beside them. Whether it&apos;s sharing supplies, covering for a comrade&apos;s mistake, or simply checking in, they prove that true leadership starts with empathy. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 49%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Bigger, louder, messier - never clean, never subtle.&lt;br&gt;- Leads with empathy. The kind we need more of.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
