			<personalityDescription>Some people call it grit, others call it madness, but Iseabal doesn&apos;t care what they think. No matter how much the world tries to grind them down, they keep going, long after anyone else would have quit. Iseabal sings because it drowns everything else out. The screams, the comm chatter, the sound of their own heartbeat pounding in their skull. If they stop singing, that means the battle&apos;s over - and that means they have to face whatever&apos;s left behind. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Grit or madness - hard to tell. Doesn&apos;t care. Just keeps moving.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
