			<personalityDescription>Andreas could probably win more fights if he didn&apos;t spend so much time starting them. Whether it&apos;s trash-talking over comms or throwing the first punch in a negotiation, he seems to believe the best way to solve a problem is by making it someone else&apos;s problem. Fist first. Andreas doesn&apos;t let rules, ethics, or principles get in the way of what he wants. If bending the truth, cutting corners, or making shady deals gives him an edge, he won&apos;t lose a wink of sleep over it. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 50%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Starts problems just to end them violently. First to swing, last to think.&lt;br&gt;- Will do anything to win. Doesnt care who gets hurt.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
