			<personalityDescription>Planning has never been Cipriano&apos;s strong suit. He follows instinct over strategy, letting adrenaline and quick thinking dictate his path. Sometimes it works, sometimes it doesn&apos;t - but either way, he never hesitates. Cipriano writes down quotes because he&apos;s afraid the voices of the past will disappear. Commanders, poets, warriors - they all left something behind. Something worth remembering. Because if their words can last, maybe - just maybe - something about him will, too. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 30%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Strategy ignored. Runs on instinct and adrenaline. Sometimes lucky, always fast.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
