			<performanceExamScore>49</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Evan isn&apos;t just a thief - they&apos;re an artist. They don&apos;t just take things; they leave people wondering if they ever really had them to begin with. Every job is clean, calculated, and impossible to trace back to them. Evan wears the uniform, the gear, the weight of the war - but none of it ever feels real. They move like they&apos;re trapped in armor that isn&apos;t their own, unsure if the person they once was is even still underneath it all. &quot;I don&apos;t know if this body was ever mine. I just know it&apos;s the only one I&apos;ve got.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Treats theft like performance art - and the whole crew&apos;s the audience.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
