			<performanceExamScore>58</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>War isn&apos;t personal for Aricia - it&apos;s a business. She weighs risks like investments, treats allies like temporary partners, and knows that in the end, survival isn&apos;t about honor - it&apos;s about profit. Aricia won&apos;t just take any weapon, &apos;Mek, or gear - she has preferences, and she sticks to them religiously. If something isn&apos;t precisely the way she likes it, she won&apos;t touch it. &quot;No. That&apos;s wrong. Too heavy, wrong grip, balance is off. Get me the right one. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 55%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Treats battle like a spreadsheet. Risk/reward to the decimal.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
