			<performanceExamScore>55</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>People want to believe Ghizala, and that&apos;s the danger. She sounds sincere, looks reliable, and acts like she has your back - until the moment it benefits her to do otherwise. Ghizala doesn&apos;t know where she picked up her habits, only that they have to be done. Before every mission, she mutters phrases in a language that isn&apos;t her, pockets a bullet casing from the last fight, and refuses to eat or drink in the last hour before deployment. &quot;What happens if you stop?&quot; someone asks. Ghizala just stares at them for an uncomfortably long time before replying, &quot;We don&apos;t want to find out.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Sounds like a friend. Acts like a liability.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
