			<personalityDescription>Once, Hosang might have wanted more, but now? He&apos;s seen too many people claw their way to the top only to die just like everyone else. Ambition is just another word for desperation, and Hosang has long since stopped caring. Hosang rarely takes others seriously, rolling his eyes at concerns he doesn&apos;t find valid. Whether it&apos;s a risky plan, a personal grievance, or a suggestion he thinks is dumb, he shuts it down with a snide remark and moves on. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 52%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Burned out or just gave up - either way, not climbing.&lt;br&gt;- Eye-rolls and shutdowns. Doesn&apos;t bother pretending to care.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
