			<personalityDescription>Zina plays by her own rules, which change depending on what benefits her most. She&apos;s not a villain - she just doesn&apos;t see the point in letting things like loyalty or honesty get in the way of a good deal or an easy victory. Zina doesn&apos;t intentionally ignore responsibilities - she just gets caught up in her own world. Whether it&apos;s distractions, forgetfulness, or a lack of organization, things tend to slip through the cracks more often than they should. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 50%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Rules bend around them - ethics don&apos;t apply.&lt;br&gt;- Forgetful or just doesn&apos;t care - still a liability.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
