			<personalityDescription>Dragutin doesn&apos;t apologize - because he never sees a reason to. Whether he&apos;s bending the rules, running his mouth, or making an outrageous demand, he does it all with absolute confidence and zero regret. Dragutin knows what he&apos;s doing, but he still asks. &quot;You sure about this plan?&quot; &quot;We&apos;re really going in now?&quot; He won&apos;t commit until someone gives him a nod, a pat on the shoulder, anything to prove he&apos;s not messing up. He&apos;s not afraid of battle - he&apos;s afraid of disappointing someone. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 48%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Never apologizes, never looks back.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
