			<performanceExamScore>64</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Melissa always seems like she&apos;s one bad moment away from snapping. Whether it&apos;s a broken piece of gear, a slow-witted subordinate, or just a long day, her irritation simmers just beneath the surface, waiting for an excuse to boil over. Melissa fills every spare scrap of paper with drawings - names carved into ruined buildings, faces half-remembered, insignias from units that no longer exist. She says she draws so she won&apos;t forget, but the way she looks at her sketches, like she&apos;s haunted by them... maybe she already has. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 67%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Complains the whole op. Still finishes first.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
