			<personalityDescription>To Laurie, hesitation is just another word for failure. They throw caution aside, charging headlong into danger with raw aggression and an utter disregard for self-preservation. If survival means second-guessing, then maybe survival isn&apos;t worth it. Money isn&apos;t just a luxury for Laurie - it&apos;s an obsession. They see every interaction as a transaction, every person as a potential asset or obstacle in their relentless pursuit of fortune. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 51%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Ignores self-preservation. Sees hesitation as death. Risk of early burnout.&lt;br&gt;- Greed isnt a flaw here - its the mission.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
