			<personalityDescription>Some people call it grit, others call it madness, but Mike doesn&apos;t care what they think. No matter how much the world tries to grind him down, he keeps going, long after anyone else would have quit. Mike believes in results, not feelings. He dismisses emotions as distractions and refuses to waste time comforting others. To him, facts, logic, and action matter - sympathy does not. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 45%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Grit or madness - hard to tell. Doesn&apos;t care. Just keeps moving.&lt;br&gt;- No room for grief. Moves on before the body hits the ground.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
