			<personalityDescription>Compromise is just another word for weakness in Muhjar&apos;s mind. She doesn&apos;t negotiate or accommodate - she dictates, expecting the world to move according to her vision, whether others like it or not. Every harsh wind feels like the bite of an old wound. Every humid jungle reminds her of the infections she barely survived. Every freezing night brings back the ghost of near-hypothermia. Muhjar&apos;s body has been through hell, and now it feels every shift in the weather like a lingering punishment. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 48%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Sees compromise as failure. Imposes vision regardless of input.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
