			<performanceExamScore>49</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Miriam isn&apos;t heartless, just detached. She doesn&apos;t feel the need to intervene, fix things, or fight for anything beyond her own survival. If someone expects her to care, they&apos;ll be sorely disappointed. Miriam doesn&apos;t forget because she&apos;s careless. She forgets because her head is already full - full of old battlefields, old mistakes, old names. There&apos;s only so much room in a person&apos;s memory, and Miriam made a choice long ago: she&apos;ll never forget the fallen, even if it means losing everything else. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Detached, not cruel - but don&apos;t count on backup.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
