			<personalityDescription>Planning has never been Tycho&apos;s strong suit. They follow instinct over strategy, letting adrenaline and quick thinking dictate their path. Sometimes it works, sometimes it doesn&apos;t - but either way, they never hesitates. Tycho&apos;s hands are steady in combat, but after the fight, when the dust settles and the dead are counted, they start to tremble. So they fold. One precise crease at a time, one careful movement after another, until the shaking stops. It doesn&apos;t erase what they&apos;ve done. But for a moment, it feels like they&apos;re creating something instead of destroying it. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 55%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Strategy ignored. Runs on instinct and adrenaline. Sometimes lucky, always fast.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
