			<personalityDescription>Ray sees morality as a luxury he can&apos;t afford. If there&apos;s a faster, more efficient way to get ahead - no matter how brutal - he&apos;ll take it without hesitation or regret. No strategy is ever good enough for Ray. He picks apart every formation, every maneuver, every decision. &quot;That&apos;s a weak flank. That exit is a death trap. This timing is off by at least three seconds.&quot; It&apos;s exhausting - but more than once, his nitpicking has saved lives. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 44%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Brutality is a shortcut - and they never hesitate to take it.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
