			<personalityDescription>There is no &quot;enough&quot; for Lewis. He grind forward, unyielding, sacrificing sleep, comfort, and even allies if necessary. Failure isn&apos;t an option - because if he stops moving, he might have to face what he&apos;s lost along the way. Lewis doesn&apos;t flinch under fire, doesn&apos;t panic when missiles rain down - but his fingers tell a different story. His nails are jagged, bitten down to near nothing, the casualty of endless waiting, briefing delays, and long hours in the scrum. It&apos;s not fear, he insists. Just something to do while the next battle looms. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 51%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Sacrifices everything for progress. Keeps moving to outrun whats behind.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
