			<personalityDescription>For Wirke, compromise is just another word for weakness. They stick to their principles, strategies, and orders with unwavering determination, even when logic - or survival - suggests a different path. Wirke doesn&apos;t just want success - they demand it. They climb over anyone in their way, cutting deals, betraying allies, and making sacrifices without hesitation. In their mind, the weak stay where they are, and the strong take what they deserve. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 52%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Sees compromise as failure. Principles trump survival instinct.&lt;br&gt;- Cuts deals, cuts throats - climbs to the top by any means.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
