			<personalityDescription>Charlie has long since stopped caring about things that don&apos;t directly affect him. Wars rage, people scheme, and alliances crumble - but to him, it&apos;s all just noise. He does what&apos;s necessary and moves on without a second thought. Charlie knows what he&apos;s doing, but he still asks. &quot;You sure about this plan?&quot; &quot;We&apos;re really going in now?&quot; He won&apos;t commit until someone gives him a nod, a pat on the shoulder, anything to prove he&apos;s not messing up. He&apos;s not afraid of battle - he&apos;s afraid of disappointing someone. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 46%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Sees war as noise. Filters everything but orders.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
