			<personalityDescription>Planning has never been Lester&apos;s strong suit. He follows instinct over strategy, letting adrenaline and quick thinking dictate his path. Sometimes it works, sometimes it doesn&apos;t - but either way, he never hesitates. Before the mission even begins, Lester has already memorized the terrain, accounted for ammo reserves, and assigned every comrade a secondary role in case the plan goes sideways. &quot;You think too much,&quot; someone mutters. He doesn&apos;t argue. Thinking too much is why he&apos;s still alive. </personalityDescription>
