			<personalityDescription>Caution is for the weak, and Duridar has no patience for it. He charges headlong into the most dangerous situations with reckless abandon, trusting skill and sheer audacity to carry him through - because hesitation gets people killed. Duridar counts enemy movements, tracks their steps, and notes the exact delay between artillery salvos. &quot;That Long Tom fires every 6.4 seconds,&quot; he mutters. &quot;We have 3.2 seconds to move.&quot; Someone scoffs - until Duridar steps out exactly on time, avoiding the blast. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Rejects caution. Relies on audacity and instinct. High survivability or quick death.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
