			<personalityDescription>Grace puts on a friendly face, but it&apos;s a survival tactic as much as anything. She knows being likable keeps people from turning on her, but deep down, she&apos;s always waiting for the moment when trust becomes a liability. Tactical formations, famous last stands, the lineage of a particular unit - she can recall all of it. One moment she&apos;s breaking down the enemy&apos;s battle doctrine, the next she&apos;s casually mentioning that their insignia has roots in some obscure rebellion from 2434. Most of her comrades don&apos;t mind - unless they&apos;re trying to focus on not dying. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 39%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Knows every name, every story. Makes people feel like they matter.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
