			<personalityDescription>War isn&apos;t personal for Julian - it&apos;s a business. He weighs risks like investments, treats allies like temporary partners, and knows that in the end, survival isn&apos;t about honor - it&apos;s about profit. Julian&apos;s war journal is supposed to be for mission notes, but it&apos;s filled with sketches of things not on the battlefield: towering trees from some distant world, the face of a woman he can&apos;t quite remember, the endless stars above the DropShip bay. Maybe he fights so one day he won&apos;t have to anymore. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Treats battle like a spreadsheet. Risk/reward to the decimal.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
