			<personalityDescription>John&apos;s instincts are razor-sharp. He can smell a bad deal before it&apos;s offered, spot a bluff before it&apos;s played, and turn a negotiation into a masterclass in getting exactly what he wants. While he doesn&apos;t seek attention, John notices everything. He listens more than he speaks, analyzes before he acts, and values deep conversations over shallow chatter. His quiet nature makes his words all the more impactful when he chooses to share them. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 54%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Born dealmaker. If they&apos;re smiling, you&apos;ve already lost something.&lt;br&gt;- Quiet type. Won&apos;t lead the toast, but will notice who&apos;s missing.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
