			<personalityDescription>The line between confidence and recklessness is one Nicholas never bothers to acknowledge. He acts on impulse, ignores warnings, and barrels forward at full speed, trusting that he&apos;ll figure things out before it&apos;s too late. Nicholas has seen people die because they settled for &quot;good enough&quot;. He refuses to make that mistake. If something isn&apos;t exactly right, it&apos;s wrong, and he won&apos;t compromise. &quot;Precision isn&apos;t optional. You think I&apos;m difficult? Fine. At least I&apos;ll still be alive.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 49%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Doesn&apos;t care if it&apos;s reckless - just that it&apos;s fast and loud.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
