			<personalityDescription>Joe doesn&apos;t just take charge - he owns every situation he steps into. His presence alone demands compliance, and he has little patience for those who hesitate to fall in line. Joe&apos;s obsessiveness isn&apos;t just habit - it&apos;s desperation. He can&apos;t stop tweaking his loadout, refining battle plans, checking his gear again and again - because the moment he stops? The moment he trusts things to go as expected? That&apos;s when people die. And he&apos;s already lost too many. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 51%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Dominates by presence alone. Expects immediate compliance.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
