			<personalityDescription>Ajitapala always has an excuse, a clever explanation, or a way to shift blame. He might sound sincere, but when push comes to shove, he&apos;ll disappear, take the better offer, or leave others holding the bag. Ajitapala refuses to throw anything away-every scrap, every trinket, every memory means something. Because war erases people. It wipes them out. And if he doesn&apos;t hold onto what little remains, who will? </personalityDescription>
