			<personalityDescription>The more dangerous the path, the more certain Kusumakar is that it&apos;s the right one. He moves forward without fear, seeing every unknown as a puzzle to solve, a victory to claim, or a story to tell later. Kusumakar doesn&apos;t do favors, fight for causes, or make sacrifices for free. If someone needs his skills, they&apos;d better be ready to pay up, because when the money stops, so does his interest. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 55%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- The harder the path, the more they want it. Danger is proof they&apos;re on track.&lt;br&gt;- Doesn&apos;t move unless the C-Bills do. Motivation ends where the payment does.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
