			<personalityDescription>Zuo-lin doesn&apos;t just think they&apos;re invincible - they act like it. They take unnecessary risks, dismisses warnings, and underestimate opponents, convinced that sheer skill (or luck) will always pull them through. One day, it won&apos;t. Zuo-lin sees through people like glass. They pick apart their motives, exploit their weaknesses, and predict their actions before they even realize what they&apos;re going to do. It&apos;s not empathy - it&apos;s just another tool for survival. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 46%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Ignores danger, overestimates skill. One day, luck will run out.&lt;br&gt;- Picks targets apart like it&apos;s instinct. Cold, fast, surgical.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
