			<personalityDescription>Argo&apos;s leadership style leaves no room for autonomy. They scrutinize every action, correct every mistake before it happens, and exert their will so thoroughly that those around them rarely get the chance to think for themselves. Argo fights without hesitation, pushes through gunfire and explosions, but the moment they see blood - their or anyone else&apos;s - their focus fractures. Their breathing changes, their grip tightens, and they force themself to look anywhere else. &quot;I&apos;m fine. I just - don&apos;t ask me to look at it.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 52%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Smothers autonomy. Others follow not by choice - but by lack of room to do otherwise.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
