			<personalityDescription>Indiana isn&apos;t interested in quick victories - she&apos;s interested in certain victories. She waits, watches, and maneuvers every piece into place before making her move, ensuring that when the moment comes, her enemies never see it coming. Subtlety has never been Indiana&apos;s strong suit. She speaks in hard facts and brutal honesty, never sugarcoating her words or wasting time on delicate phrasing. If someone doesn&apos;t like it, that&apos;s their problem. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 36%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Prefers certainty to speed. Strikes only when the board is set.&lt;br&gt;- Subtle as artillery. Doesnt care who flinches.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
