			<personalityDescription>Joan doesn&apos;t waste time on moral debates - they do what needs to be done. If that means breaking promises, cutting corners, or stepping over someone to get ahead, so be it. Joan doesn&apos;t deal in half-truths or carefully worded pleasantries. They call things exactly as they see them, no matter how uncomfortable it makes people - because, to them, honesty is more valuable than diplomacy. </personalityDescription>
