			<personalityDescription>Virgílio is convinced he&apos;s the best warrior, the best tactician, and probably the smartest person in the room. He doesn&apos;t just believe in himself - he assumes everyone else is playing catch-up, whether they realize it or not. Virgílio doesn&apos;t trust command, strategy reports, or maps drawn by people who have never stepped foot here. He trusts locals. He knows that understanding them is the difference between life and death. &quot;You ignore them, you die. It&apos;s that simple. And when you do, they won&apos;t mourn you. They&apos;ll say you deserved it.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 33%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Assumes superiority in everything. Believes others are just trying to catch up.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
