			<personalityDescription>A constant storm of anger simmers beneath Lloyd&apos;s surface, ready to explode at the slightest provocation. They don&apos;t just despise their enemies - they barely tolerates allies, seeing them as temporary conveniences rather than comrades. While they don&apos;t seek attention, Lloyd notices everything. They listen more than they speak, analyze before they act, and value deep conversations over shallow chatter. Their quiet nature makes their words all the more impactful when they choose to share them. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 49%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Anger always close to the surface. Barely tolerates allies - expects them to fail.&lt;br&gt;- Quiet type. Won&apos;t lead the toast, but will notice who&apos;s missing.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
