			<personalityDescription>Colm&apos;s leadership style leaves no room for autonomy. He scrutinizes every action, corrects every mistake before it happens, and exerts his will so thoroughly that those around him rarely get the chance to think for themselves. Colm doesn&apos;t just look down on others - he barely acknowledges them. He sees most people as incompetent, useless, or beneath him, and he makes no effort to hide his disdain. If someone disagrees with him, he assumes they&apos;re simply too stupid to understand. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 45%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Smothers autonomy. Others follow not by choice - but by lack of room to do otherwise.&lt;br&gt;- Doesn&apos;t debate - dismisses. Everyone else? Background noise.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
