			<personalityDescription>There&apos;s no room for hesitation in Vasudhara&apos;s world. She steps forward without looking back, her decisions made with the kind of conviction that leaves little space for argument. Whether she&apos;s right or wrong, she never lingers in uncertainty. Vasudhara&apos;s hesitation isn&apos;t a flaw - it&apos;s the weight of too many failures, too many ghosts whispering in her ear. Every decision echoes the last mistake, and sometimes the fear of being wrong keeps her from acting at all. &quot;I&apos;ve seen what happens when you make the wrong call. Sometimes standing still feels safer.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 51%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Decides quickly and moves on. Doesn&apos;t second-guess, right or wrong.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
