			<personalityDescription>Martina gives because she knows what it&apos;s like to have nothing. She&apos;ll take the hard jobs, give up her share, and put herself in danger for the sake of others - even when it costs her more than she can afford to lose. Martina hands out nicknames like candy. It&apos;s easier than remembering real names - because real names come with memories. With losses. With faces she&apos;d rather not picture when she tries to sleep. As long as they&apos;re &apos;Deadeye&apos; or &apos;Hellhound&apos; or &apos;Bulldozer&apos;, she doesn&apos;t have to think about how many real names she&apos;s already forgotten. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 38%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Gives more than they should. Probably won&apos;t stop until it breaks them.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
