			<personalityDescription>Jayla doesn&apos;t measure risk the way others do. Where they see danger, she sees duty; where others hesitate, she moves forward. Not because she doesn&apos;t feel fear, but because she refuses to let it define her. Jayla doesn&apos;t waste time on moral debates. If cutting corners or bending the rules gets the job done faster, she&apos;ll do it without hesitation. Her comrades have learned not to ask how she pulls off certain victories. &quot;Look, I got the result we needed. Let&apos;s not ruin it by asking too many questions.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 48%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Sees duty, not danger. Fear present - but doesn&apos;t get a say.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
