			<personalityDescription>Philip is convinced he&apos;s the best warrior, the best tactician, and probably the smartest person in the room. He doesn&apos;t just believe in himself - he assumes everyone else is playing catch-up, whether they realize it or not. War isn&apos;t personal for Philip - it&apos;s a business. He weighs risks like investments, treats allies like temporary partners, and knows that in the end, survival isn&apos;t about honor - it&apos;s about profit. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 54%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Assumes superiority in everything. Believes others are just trying to catch up.&lt;br&gt;- Treats battle like a spreadsheet. Risk/reward to the decimal.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
