			<personalityDescription>Indecision is just another form of weakness, and Domingo refuses to entertain it. He makes the call, moves forward, and never looks back - because in the brutal reality of war, second-guessing gets people killed. No matter how many times Domingo gets knocked down, he gets back up stronger. He takes every hit, every loss, every failure, and turns it into fuel to keep moving forward. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 43%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Sees hesitation as lethal. Makes the call, never looks back. Hard charger.&lt;br&gt;- Uses every failure as fuel. Stronger after every fall.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
