			<personalityDescription>Madhurima is convinced she can handle anything, no matter how big the challenge. She stretches herself thin, takes on risks she shouldn&apos;t, and charges ahead without thinking about whether she can actually pull it off - because failure isn&apos;t part of her vocabulary. Yet. Madhurima never gives a straight answer. She dodges questions, avoids commitments, and keeps people guessing about where she really stands. It&apos;s not outright lying - it&apos;s just never letting anyone get close enough to see the truth. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 45%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Thinks confidence replaces planning. Runs headfirst into collapse.&lt;br&gt;- Never commits. Just enough truth to stay slippery.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
