			<personalityDescription>Kája plays by their own rules, which change depending on what benefits them most. They&apos;re not a villain - they just don&apos;t see the point in letting things like loyalty or honesty get in the way of a good deal or an easy victory. Kája always has an excuse, a clever explanation, or a way to shift blame. They might sound sincere, but when push comes to shove, they&apos;ll disappear, take the better offer, or leave others holding the bag. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Rules bend around them - ethics don&apos;t apply.&lt;br&gt;- Slippery. Never in the wrong, never where you left them.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
