			<personalityDescription>Ugo sees war for what it is - a business. He&apos;s a professional, not a hero, and he takes jobs that make sense, get him paid, and keep him alive. He doesn&apos;t fight for glory; he fights to make sure he sees another payday. Ugo doesn&apos;t believe in standard color schemes or obvious silhouettes. His equipment always matches the terrain - dust-covered in deserts, ice-slicked in tundras, urban-camouflaged in cities. &quot;Standing out is just asking to get shot first.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 54%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Fights smart, not proud. Prioritizes payday over valor.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
