			<performanceExamScore>54</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Seong-rae doesn&apos;t just look down on others - he barely acknowledges them. He sees himself as superior in every way, treating allies as tools and enemies as annoyances. If someone disagrees with him, it&apos;s because they&apos;re too stupid to understand why he&apos;s right. Seong-rae clears every building like it&apos;s booby-trapped, refuses to fire unless he&apos;s sure it&apos;s a clean shot, and won&apos;t step forward unless he&apos;s positive about footing. &quot;We don&apos;t have time for this,&quot; someone groans. &quot;We don&apos;t have time to die stupidly, either,&quot; Seong-rae shoots back. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Barely acknowledges teammates. Sees people as tools or distractions.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
