			<personalityDescription>Keeping up with details isn&apos;t a priority for Szu-I. She does the bare minimum to get by, leaving others to pick up the slack. Whether it&apos;s out of laziness or indifference, she rarely follows through unless it directly benefits her. Szu-I doesn&apos;t just fight - she plays a role. She wants her last stand to be legendary, her name whispered in hushed tones long after she&apos;s gone. If she falls, it has to be in a blaze of glory, outnumbered but never outmatched. The problem is... war doesn&apos;t care about theatrics. And no one remembers the dead the way they think they will. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Bare minimum effort. Team carries the rest.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
