			<performanceExamScore>45</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>There&apos;s no such thing as overconfidence in Bari&apos;s mind. Whether he&apos;s got the skills to back it up or not is irrelevant - he steps into every situation like he&apos;s already won and lets reality catch up later. Bari doesn&apos;t just see territory - he sees people. Whenever he&apos;s deployed, he learns the culture, the customs, the stories of those who live there. He doesn&apos;t believe in fighting blindly. &quot;You want to survive out here? Then talk to the ones who actually live here - they&apos;ve been surviving longer than we have.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 50%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Confidence exceeds ability. May succeed through force of will - or get others killed.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
