			<personalityDescription>Patience is just wasted time in Wagih&apos;s eyes. He meets every challenge head-on, cutting through hesitation with sheer force of will. The only direction that matters is forward, and anything in his way is just another problem to crush. Strategy and logic have their place, but Wagih thrives on instinct. He senses the right moment to strike, the subtle shifts in an opponent&apos;s stance, the unseen dangers lurking just out of sight - always a step ahead without knowing how he knows. They just do. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 70%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Patience dismissed as weakness. Crushes obstacles with brute force.&lt;br&gt;- Sees what&apos;s about to happen like it already did. Relies on feel, not fact.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
