			<personalityDescription>Tormey doesn&apos;t waste time on moral debates - he does what needs to be done. If that means breaking promises, cutting corners, or stepping over someone to get ahead, so be it. Tormey actively avoids any situation that might require zero gravity. If there&apos;s a job that needs to be done weightless, he&apos;s already volunteering someone else. &quot;I&apos;ll take the next shift. On the ground. Where things stay where they&apos;re supposed to be.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 47%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Gets results, not approval - steps over whoever&apos;s in the way.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
