			<personalityDescription>Caution is for the slow and the dead, and Hombert refuses to be either. He rushes headlong into danger, making split-second decisions that could be called bravery - or  sheer madness. One way or another, Hombert never stands still. Hombert doesn&apos;t trust dimly lit rooms. If a bulb flickers, he notices immediately. If he&apos;s in a dark space for too long, he starts looking for any excuse to bring in more light. &quot;No, I don&apos;t think it&apos;s &apos;cozy&apos; - I think it&apos;s a goddamn liability.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 49%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Rejects caution. Speed over safety. Bravery or recklessness - depends on the day.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
