			<personalityDescription>Fouad believes leadership isn&apos;t about consensus - it&apos;s about control. He doesn&apos;t ask for loyalty; he assumes it, and those who resist quickly learn that standing in his way is never a good idea. Fouad&apos;s writing is rough, unpolished, but deeply personal. He doesn&apos;t care if it&apos;s perfect - he just wants it to feel real. &quot;I&apos;m not writing for anyone else. If you don&apos;t like it, don&apos;t read it.&quot; </personalityDescription>
