			<performanceExamScore>49</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Violence isn&apos;t just a tool for Kara - it&apos;s the default setting. She sees every interaction as a challenge, every stare as a provocation, and every battle as a chance to break something... or someone. Peace is just the pause before the next conflict. Kara customizes everything because she&apos;s seen too many things fail when they shouldn&apos;t. People trust that things will work the way they&apos;re designed. Kara  knows better. If she built it, if she reinforced it, then at least she knows it won&apos;t fail the moment it&apos;s needed most </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 50%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Interprets peace as waiting room for violence. Every glance is a challenge.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
