			<performanceExamScore>55</performanceExamScore>
			<personalityDescription>Hada prefers to observe rather than dominate a conversation. She speaks when necessary, keeps her thoughts to herself, and tends to recharge best when she&apos;s alone rather than in a crowd. Hada doesn&apos;t fear technology because she doesn&apos;t understand it - she fears it because she understands it too well. She&apos;s seen what happens when an IFF controlled turret malfunctions, when a faulty suit seal dooms a pilot to vacuum, when a simple software patch bricks a JumpShip&apos;s entire navigation systems. Technology doesn&apos;t fail quietly. It fails with screams. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 54%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Doesn&apos;t talk much - listens to everything.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
