			<personalityDescription>Makoto doesn&apos;t believe in sharing, trusting, or sacrificing for others. The universe is cruel, and only those who look out for themselves survive. If someone expects him to stick his neck out for them, they&apos;re in for a rude awakening. Makoto doesn&apos;t believe in complicated tactics. If something can&apos;t be explained in one sentence, he doesn&apos;t trust it. He values direct execution over drawn-out planning and believes the simplest strategies are usually the ones that actually succeed. </personalityDescription>
