			<personalityDescription>Tressa doesn&apos;t deal in half-truths or carefully worded pleasantries. She calls things exactly as she sees them, no matter how uncomfortable it makes people - because, to her, honesty is more valuable than diplomacy. Tressa doesn&apos;t just stretch - she needs to. The stress, the exhaustion, the pressure - her body takes it all in. So she moves, keeps things loose, because if her joints lock up, she might realize just how much damage she&apos;s actually taken. </personalityDescription>
