			<personalityDescription>Kunegundy isn&apos;t satisfied with victory - she demands eradication. To her, an enemy left standing is an enemy that wasn&apos;t taught the right lesson, and she has no interest in teaching it twice. Kunegundy approaches everything with methodical precision. She doesn&apos;t believe in shortcuts or luck - only in putting in the work, refining her craft, and ensuring that she never leaves anything to chance. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 51%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Victory is incomplete if anything survives. Believes lessons should be final.&lt;br&gt;- Methodical and tireless. Trusts hard work over luck every time.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
