			<personalityDescription>Nothing Julie does is by chance - they play the long game, reading between the lines and thinking five steps ahead. By the time others realize what&apos;s happening, they&apos;ve already won. Once, Julie might have cared. Now, they just drift. Wars rage, alliances shift, people come and go, and none of it moves them. They do what&apos;s necessary to get by, but passion and purpose are long-forgotten luxuries. </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 53%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Always several moves ahead. Opponents realize too late they&apos;ve lost.&lt;br&gt;- Burned out long before we met them. Just ash in uniform.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
