			<personalityDescription>Diana&apos;s mind is razor-sharp, cutting through noise and distractions to find the truth hidden beneath. She notices patterns, anticipates outcomes, and always seems to be one step ahead of the game. Diana sees long-range engagements as impersonal, inefficient, and, worst of all, boring. She thrives where things are fast, brutal, and decided in seconds. &quot;If I&apos;m fighting,&quot; she says, cracking her knuckles, &quot;I want them to know it was me.&quot; </personalityDescription>
			<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 50%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Filters out the noise. Cuts straight to what matters.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
