				<performanceExamScore>48</performanceExamScore>
				<personalityDescription>Maaria&apos;s indifference isn&apos;t an act - it&apos;s survival. She&apos;s seen too much, lost too much, and learned that the only way to endure is to stop feeling altogether. The universe burns, but she stopped worrying about the flames a long time ago. Maaria knows holovids are escapism, but she doesn&apos;t care. They&apos;re structured, predictable, full of meaning. Unlike the mess that is real life, where nothing follows a script and everything falls apart for no reason. &quot;Real life&apos;s got terrible pacing. At least in holovids, things happen for a reason.&quot; </personalityDescription>
				<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 45%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Hollow eyes. Doesnt hate you - just can&apos;t be bothered to.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
