				<performanceExamScore>54</performanceExamScore>
				<personalityDescription>José can sell a rusted-out &apos;Mek for triple its value and walk away smiling. He spins stories, plays up his credentials, and always has an answer ready when someone starts asking too many questions. By the time people realize they&apos;ve been had, he&apos;s long gone. José makes clothes because it&apos;s something tangible, something he can control when everything else feels like it&apos;s spiraling. The fact that people wear his work means a part of him is protecting them, even when he&apos;s not there. &quot;If you&apos;re going to bleed, you might as well bleed in something that fits.&quot; </personalityDescription>
				<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 48%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Could sell ice to polar troops and vanish before the melt.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
