				<performanceExamScore>51</performanceExamScore>
				<personalityDescription>Lisa treats the impossible like an invitation. She never slows down, never looks back, and never lets fear dictate her choices - because, to her, fear is just an excuse she refuses to entertain. Lisa doesn&apos;t trust command, strategy reports, or maps drawn by people who have never stepped foot here. She trusts locals. She knows that understanding them is the difference between life and death. &quot;You ignore them, you die. It&apos;s that simple. And when you do, they won&apos;t mourn you. They&apos;ll say you deserved it.&quot; </personalityDescription>
				<personalityInterviewNotes>&lt;html&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Exam:&lt;/b&gt; 48%&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Fear doesn&apos;t factor in. Treats the impossible like a dare.&lt;/html&gt;</personalityInterviewNotes>
